<title>JAPAN: Japan jobless rate falls to 3.3 pct in August.</title>
<headline>Japan jobless rate falls to 3.3 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate fell to 3.3 percent in August from 3.4 percent in July, while the closely watched jobs-to-applicants ratio fell to 0.71 from 0.72 the previous month, the government announced on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the job data follows.</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			Aug	July	Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	     3.3 pct   3.4 pct    3.2 pct</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio    0.71	0.72	 0.61</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)		    Aug	 July	 Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	     3.3 pct   3.2 pct    3.2 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	  2.24 million  2.21 million   2.16 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		  Aug	     Year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				 65.42 million    +0.7 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p>  Manufacturing			14.52 million    -0.8 pct</p>
<p>  Services			     15.97 million    +0.8 pct</p>
<p>  Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.68 million    +2.4 pct</p>
<p>  Construction			  6.81 million    +3.8 pct</p>
<p>  Agriculture			   3.68 million    -2.9 pct</p>
</text>
